==German==

===Etymology===
Neologism coined in 1999 in analogy to {{m|de|satt|t=not hungry anymore}} as part of a collaborative contest between {{w|Duden}} and {{w|Lipton}}. Out of the 45000 suggestions, '''sitt''' has been suggested 40 times.<ref>[https://www.ata-divisions.org/GLD/docs/inter_archive/2000_03.pdf#page=8 Manfred Winter, March 2000, ''Sitt und satt!'']</ref><ref>[https://www.welt.de/print-welt/article586866/Genug-getrunken-Duden-Redaktion-Dann-ist-man-sitt.html welt.de, 08.10.1999, ''Genug getrunken? Duden-Redaktion: "Dann ist man sitt"'']</ref> It has however never seen widespread use.

